---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const personas = [
  { name: 'The Operator', take: 'Will this help someone run a team or a business on Monday?' },
  { name: 'The Professor', take: 'Is it rigorous, original and influential in its field?' },
  { name: 'The Skeptic', take: 'Does it rest on evidence, or on stories and fluff?' },
  { name: 'The Mindset Coach', take: 'Does it change how a reader thinks and acts?' },
  { name: 'The Modernist', take: 'Does it still matter in an AI-shaped world?' },
  { name: "The Reader's Advocate", take: 'Is it clear, readable and worth the time?' },
];
---

<Base title="How it's made" description="How 365 Books picks, writes, checks and tags each summary.">
  <article class="container page">
    <header>
      <p class="label">Method</p>
      <h1>How it's made</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        365 business books in 12 themes, released in batches. Every summary is written by AI, and this
        page explains exactly how.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-header"><span class="num">01</span> / Selection</h2>
      <p>
        Each theme starts with a long list drawn from public best-of lists, Claude's own nominations
        from the canon, and 3 to 5 wildcard picks from each panel persona. Every candidate gets two
        scores from 1 to 5: a weighted rubric score and a panel score (the average of six personas).
        The final score is the average of the two.
      </p>
      <p>
        Books near the cutoff go to a debate, which also settles overlaps, author caps and theme
        placement. Each book appears in one theme only.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-header"><span class="num">02</span> / The panel</h2>
      <ul class="personas">
        {personas.map((p) => (
          <li><strong>{p.name}</strong><span>{p.take}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        The personas and all scores are Claude's judgment, not data. Every book page shows its persona
        scorecard under "How it made the list".
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-header"><span class="num">03</span> / Writing</h2>
      <p>
        Summaries describe each book in the third person, in the book's own flavor, never as the author
        speaking. Each one quotes the book at most twice, briefly, and only with verified quotes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The AI-era lens is separate and labeled <span class="ai-badge">AI analysis</span>. It uses one
        house voice and never guesses what an author thinks about AI. It tags every key concept:
      </p>
      <dl class="verdicts">
        <div><dt><span class="tag tag--transcends">Transcends</span></dt><dd>Holds up as is, or matters more because of AI.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><span class="tag tag--evolves">Evolves</span></dt><dd>The principle holds, but how you apply it changes.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><span class="tag tag--expires">Expires</span></dt><dd>Tied to a way of working that AI is replacing.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-header"><span class="num">04</span> / Verification</h2>
      <p>
        Before a summary counts as verified, a separate review pass checks it against outside sources
        and corrects what it can't confirm. Each page lists its sources, what the review changed, and a
        confidence level (high or medium).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-header"><span class="num">05</span> / AI disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        The summaries, the AI-era lens and the scores are written by Claude (Anthropic). Joe chooses the
        themes, approves each batch, and reads the books over time as
        <a href={url('/reader-zero/')}>reader zero</a>. A summary is not a substitute for reading the
        book. If you spot an error, use "Report a correction" at the bottom of any book page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 48px; }
  .page header .lead { margin-top: 24px; max-width: 760px; }
  .page p { max-width: 72ch; }
  .num { color: var(--text); }
  .personas {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .personas li { background: var(--bg); padding: 16px 20px; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .personas span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .verdicts { margin: 16px 0 0; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .verdicts div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr; gap: 16px; align-items: baseline; }
  .verdicts dt, .verdicts dd { margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .personas { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .verdicts div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
  }
</style>
